sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To draw a straight line through a given point parallel to a given straight line.
----
proof:

Let {A} be the given point, and {BC} the given straight line.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="230" height="160" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="I.31 diagram" src="propI31.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "I.31",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;130,40",
            "B;point;free;40,120",
            "C;point;free;180,120",
            "D;point;lineSlider;B,C,100,120",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "AE;line;similar;A,D,D,A,C",
            "E;point;last;AE",
            "AF;line;extend;E,A,B,D",
            "F;point;last;AF",
            // Zero-color hover target for the whole constructed parallel
            // E–A–F (so {EF} / {EAF} light the full line through A; it is
            // drawn visibly as AE + AF).
            "EF;line;connect;E,F;0;0;0",
            // The alternate angles AD makes (#91): the copied ∠EAD (=∠DAE) at
            // A and the original ∠ADC at D. Distinct vertices, no #103 nesting.
            "EAD;sector;angleMarker;A,E,D",
            "ADC;sector;angleMarker;D,A,C"
        ],
        aliases: { "DAE": "EAD", "EAF": "EF" },
        deferDraggables: ["D"],
        slides: [
            { text: "Let {A} be the given point, and {BC} the given straight line.",
              visible: ["BC"],
              highlighted: ["A","BC"] },
            { text: "It is required to draw a straight line through the point {A} parallel to the straight line {BC}.",
              visible: ["BC"],
              highlighted: ["A","BC"] },
            { text: "Take a point {D} at random on {BC}. Join {AD}.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD"],
              highlighted: ["D","AD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "D",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "AD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Construct the angle {DAE} equal to the angle {ADC} on the straight line {DA} and at the point {A} on it.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD","AE","E","ADC","EAD"],
              highlighted: ["EAD","ADC","AE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "ADC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "AE",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "EAD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "Produce the straight line {AF} in a straight line with {EA}.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD","AE","E","ADC","EAD","AF","F"],
              highlighted: ["AF"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "AF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.2" }] },
            { text: "Since the straight line {AD} falling on the two straight lines {BC} and {EF} makes the alternate angles {EAD} and {ADC} equal to one another, therefore {EAF} is parallel to {BC}.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD","AE","E","ADC","EAD","AF","F","EF"],
              highlighted: ["AD","BC","EF","EAD","ADC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.27" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the straight line {EAF} has been drawn through the given point {A} parallel to the given straight line {BC}.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD","AE","E","ADC","EAD","AF","F","EF"],
              highlighted: ["EF","A","BC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.Post.2": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post2/",
        "I.23":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI23/",
        "I.27":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI27/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

It is required to draw a straight line through the point {A} parallel to the straight line {BC}.

Take a point {D} at random on {BC}. Join {AD}. Construct the angle {DAE} equal to the angle {ADC} on the straight line {DA} and at the point {A} on it. Produce the straight line {AF} in a straight line with {EA}. [!just I.Post.1; I.23; I.Post.2]

Since the straight line {AD} falling on the two straight lines {BC} and {EF} makes the alternate angles {EAD} and {ADC} equal to one another, therefore {EAF} is parallel to {BC}. [!just I.27]

Therefore the straight line {EAF} has been drawn through the given point {A} parallel to the given straight line {BC}.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide:

The parallel line {EF} constructed in this proposition is the only one passing through the point {A}. If there were another, then the interior angles on one side or the other of {AD} it makes with {BC} would be less than two right angles, and therefore by the parallel postulate @I.Post.5, it would meet {BC}, a contradiction.

Incidentally, this construction also works in hyperbolic geometry, although different parallel lines through {A} are constructed for different points {D}.

#### Construction steps

The construction needed is that of @I.23 to construct an angle. That construction required ten circles and one line in general. In the specific case needed here, however, one of the distances does not have to be transferred, and that eliminates the need to construct four of the circles. Therefore this construction actually only requires six circles and a line.

The walk below carries out that specialized copy of the angle, and counts the six circles at the end.

<figure class="diagram rdiagram">
<canvas id="canvas_1" width="380" height="320" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="I.31 six-circle construction" src="propI31.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_1",
        background: "0,0,100",
        title: "I.31 — six circles",
        elements: [
            "D;point;free;90,150",
            "A;point;free;150,100",
            "C;point;free;250,150",
            // The given angle at D (rays only), copied onto the line AD at A.
            "sideDA;line;connect;D,A;0;0;black",
            "sideDC;line;connect;D,C;0;0;black",
            // P on ray DC with DP = DA, found where K1 meets DC (hidden helper).
            "P;point;cutoff;D,C,D,A",
            // Zero-color hover targets (drawn only when a caption phrase is
            // hovered): the join DP and the chord AP, both intermediate lines.
            "DP;line;connect;D,P;0;0;0",
            "AP;line;connect;A,P;0;0;0",
            // --- FOUR circles transfer the chord PA to the centre D (I.1 + I.2).
            // I.1 equilateral triangle on DP: the two circles K1, K2 meet at apex
            // T. K1 (centre D, radius DA) also cuts DC at P — so no separate
            // equal-sides circle is drawn.
            "K1;circle;radius;D,P;0;0;black;0",
            "K2;circle;radius;P,D;0;0;black;0",
            "TT;line;bichord;K1,K2;0;0;0",
            "T;point;first;TT",
            "TPx;point;extend;T,P,T,P;0;0",
            "TDx;point;extend;T,D,T,D;0;0",
            // Zero-color hover target for the produced side TP: apex T through
            // P, past G to TPx (drawn only when its caption phrase is hovered).
            "TPprod;line;connect;T,TPx;0;0;0",
            // I.2 lay-off: K3 (centre P, radius PA) marks G on the produced TP;
            // K4 (centre T, radius TG) carries that length round to the produced
            // TD, so the transferred length lands at D.
            "G;point;cutoff;P,TPx,P,A",
            "K3;circle;radius;P,A;0;0;black;0",
            "K4;circle;radius;T,G;0;0;black;0",
            // --- TWO result circles: centre A radius the side already in place,
            // centre D radius the chord.
            "Acirc;circle;radius;A,D;0;0;black;0",
            "Gcirc;circle;radius;D,A,P;0;0;black;0",
            // Apex F = Acirc ∩ Gcirc, and THE ONE LINE, AF.
            "FF;line;bichord;Acirc,Gcirc;0;0;0",
            "F;point;first;FF",
            "AF;line;connect;A,F",
            // The OTHER intersection of the two result circles — the mirror of
            // F across AD. It gives the same angle but on C's side, so AF2 is
            // NOT parallel; shown (red) to demonstrate why the fixed choice of
            // F matters when A is dragged across DC.
            "F2;point;last;FF;red;red",
            "AF2;line;connect;A,F2;0;0;red",
            // Angle markers for the illustrative slides only: the given angle
            // at D, the copied FAD (alternate -> parallel) and the mirror F2AD
            // (same side -> not parallel). Radii pinned to dodge #103 nesting.
            "angADC;sector;angleMarker;D,A,C",
            "angFAD;sector;angleMarker;A,F,D,22",
            "angF2AD;sector;angleMarker;A,F2,D,22"
        ],
        // Resting/static canvas = the slide-9 view (the angle, the two result
        // circles, AF and the F/F2 comparison). The busy six-circle scaffolding
        // is hidden at rest and only revealed by stepping through the slides;
        // clearVisibility restores this baseline on exit. (Angle markers are
        // already hidden at rest by #100.)
        initiallyHidden: ["P","T","G","K1","K2","K3","K4"],
        slides: [
            { text: "This is the construction of I.23 to copy an angle, applied to the angle at {D}. Because the {side|sideDA} from {D} to {A} already lies along the line, that distance need not be transferred — four of the ten circles are eliminated, leaving six.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC"],
              highlighted: ["sideDA","sideDC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "{Circle|K1} 1 — centre {D}, through {A}. It is the first circle of the equilateral triangle (Prop I.1) that begins the transfer, and it cuts the {ray|sideDC} toward {C} at {P}, so {P} lies as far from {D} as {A} does.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","K1","P"],
              highlighted: ["K1","P"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "K1", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "P",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.1" }] },
            { text: "{Circle|K2} 2 — centre {P}, through {D}. With {circle|K1} 1 it completes the equilateral triangle on the {join|DP}, the two circles meeting at the apex {T}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","K1","P","DP","K2","T"],
              highlighted: ["K2","T"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "K2", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "T",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "{Circle|K3} 3 — centre {P}, through {A}. Its radius is the {chord|AP} from {A} to {P}, the third distance of the angle. It cuts the {side|TPprod} produced from the apex {T} through {P} at {G}, so that {P}–{G} equals the chord — laying that length on a line through {T}, ready for the next circle to swing round to {D}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","K1","P","K2","T","K3","G","AP","TPprod"],
              highlighted: ["K3","G"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "K3", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "G",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "{Circle|K4} 4 — centre {T}, through {G}. It carries that length around to the produced side through {D}, so a length equal to the {chord|AP} from {A} to {P} now reaches from {D}. These four circles are the transfer, by Propositions I.1 and I.2.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","K1","P","K2","T","K3","G","K4","AP"],
              highlighted: ["K4"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "K4", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.1" }, { ref: "I.2" }] },
            { text: "{Circle|Acirc} 5 — centre {A}, through {D}: the first result circle. The new side must equal the {side|sideDA} already in place, so its far end will lie on this {circle|Acirc}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","K1","P","K2","T","K3","G","K4","Acirc"],
              highlighted: ["Acirc"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "Acirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] } },
            { text: "{Circle|Gcirc} 6 — centre {D}, with radius the transferred {chord|AP}: the second result circle. The far end of the new side must be the chord's length from {D}, so it will lie on this {circle|Gcirc} too.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","K1","P","K2","T","K3","G","K4","Acirc","Gcirc","AP"],
              highlighted: ["Gcirc"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "Gcirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] } },
            { text: "{Circle|Acirc} 5 and {circle|Gcirc} 6 meet at the point {F}, and the new {side|AF} is the other side of the required angle — equal to the angle at {D}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","K1","P","K2","T","K3","G","K4","Acirc","Gcirc","F","AF"],
              highlighted: ["Acirc","Gcirc","F","AF"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "F",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "AF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "The choice of {F} matters. {Circle|Acirc} 5 and {circle|Gcirc} 6 meet at two points: we take {F}, on the far side of {AD|sideDA} from {C}, so {AF} runs parallel to {DC|sideDC}. The other meeting point, {F2}, gives the same angle mirrored, so {AF2} crosses {DC|sideDC} and is not parallel. Drag {A} across {DC|sideDC} and the two swap roles — the parallel side is always the intersection on the far side of {AD|sideDA} from {C}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","Acirc","Gcirc","F","AF","F2","AF2"],
              highlighted: ["F","AF","F2","AF2"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "F2",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "AF2", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Why {F} and not {F2}? Both copied angles {FAD|angFAD} and {F2AD|angF2AD} equal the given {ADC|angADC} — but only {FAD|angFAD}, on the far side of {AD|sideDA}, is the alternate angle, so only {AF} is parallel to {DC|sideDC} (I.27). {F2AD|angF2AD} sits on {C}'s side, so {AF2} is not.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","F","AF","F2","AF2","angADC","angFAD","angF2AD"],
              highlighted: ["angADC","angFAD","angF2AD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angADC",  name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angFAD",  name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angF2AD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.27" }] },
            { text: "In all there are six circles and one {line|AF} that must be drawn. The intermediate lines may be suppressed, since they only serve to verify the construction.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","P","T","G","F","AF","K1","K2","K3","K4","Acirc","Gcirc"],
              highlighted: ["AF","K1","K2","K3","K4","Acirc","Gcirc"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AF",    name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "K1",    name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "K2",    name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "K3",    name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "K4",    name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "Acirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "Gcirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] } }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.1":  "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI1/",
        "I.2":  "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI2/",
        "I.23": "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI23/",
        "I.27": "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI27/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

#### Use of Proposition 31

This construction is frequently used in the remainder of Book I starting with the next proposition. It is also frequently used in Books II, IV, VI, XI, XII, and XIII.
